{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n '\"'^#|''^##|''^###|OD-[123]|invariant|identity|outcome|cursor|gap'\"' docs/design/dao.stream.md\"","aggregated_output":"1:# DaoStream Design\n7:## Purpose\n10:invariants of [`datom.world.md`](./datom.world.md). Two axioms bear on it\n41:3. A **logical-stream identity** is transport-independent plain data shared by\n44:   stream; it includes the logical-stream identity but is not that identity.\n45:5. A **cursor** is immutable interpreter-owned observation state for one\n49:identity. A handle is not portable identity. A cursor is not handle-owned\n52:Seven operations range over them, each returning an outcome map (see\n57:| `create!`    | creation specification | handle outcome     |\n58:| `attach!`    | portable descriptor    | handle outcome     |\n59:| `descriptor` | handle                 | descriptor outcome |\n60:| `cursor`     | handle, anchor         | cursor outcome     |\n61:| `next`       | handle, cursor         | read outcome       |\n62:| `append!`    | handle, value          | write outcome      |\n63:| `close!`     | handle                 | close outcome      |\n69:## Invariants\n72:- Reading is non-destructive. A reader advances its own cursor, not the stream.\n73:- Multiple cursors may observe the same retained value independently.\n74:- Interpreters own cursors and decide when to call `next`.\n78:- Retention may be bounded. A cursor over evicted history receives a gap\n79:  outcome as data; the reader decides what missing data means.\n80:- All expected operational outcomes are data, not exceptions or callbacks.\n85:- A logical stream has an identity that is plain data, the same through every\n87:  Projecting that identity never fails.\n89:Every clause below must be consistent with these invariants, and most derive\n93:that contradicts an invariant does not belong in this contract; one that merely\n96:## Result Convention\n100:- Each operation