{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_16","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'dao.stream.serving|postage|peer.*ident|kickoff' docs/design/dao.stream.discovery.md docs/design/datom.world.md src/cljc/dao/stream/serving.cljc\"","aggregated_output":"docs/design/dao.stream.discovery.md:72:The kickoff hash *is* the name. A stream announces its signed head into the DHT under\ndocs/design/dao.stream.discovery.md:74:the key the kickoff commits to. No authority exists because none is needed — the name\ndocs/design/dao.stream.discovery.md:89:[e :dir/stream  <bobs-kickoff>  t m]\ndocs/design/dao.stream.discovery.md:92:[e :dir/delegate <dir-kickoff>  t m]\ndocs/design/dao.stream.discovery.md:159:- **Paying to deposit** — a tiny flat cost to announce (Hashcash, postage).\ndocs/design/dao.stream.discovery.md:224:1. **Signed heads / kickoff-hash identity** (a stream-layer prerequisite, not\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/serving.cljc:1:(ns dao.stream.serving\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
