{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_27","type":"agent_message","text":"Completed-GMT: 2026-09-25 12:05:26 GMT\nCompleted-Local: 2026-09-25 19:05:26 Asia/Ho_Chi_Minh\n\nQ1 | **As designed: outbound `ok`, source outcome on the event medium** | The alternative would return `full` while the source might already have appended, contradicting `full`’s “nothing was appended” meaning. Amend UCF so a served `:put` resumes only on a correlated source `ok`; an unanswered append must remain distinguishable from a refused one. | [dao.stream.md:562](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/dao.stream.md:562), [dao.stream.md:570](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/dao.stream.md:570), [yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:553](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:553) | **high**. **Fable: stand**, conditional on carrying the in-flight correlation and unknown-effect state through migration. Depends on Q5’s OD-2 decision.\n\nQ2 | **Defer held reads from v1** | They save round trips, but add server demand state and repeated source polls without changing read correctness. Settle the proxy’s basic read semantics first. | [dao.stream.md:538](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/dao.stream.md:538), [Fable design:129](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1790335900000-architect-dao-stream-serving-spec.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:129) | **med**. **Fable: do not stand**; this is an optional optimization.\n\nQ3 | **Self-certifying from the start, with proof of control at registration** | A hash-shaped peer name alone proves nothing: an open relay routing by string equality can bind that name to the wrong registrant. Keep peer identity distinct from the served stream’s logical identity. | [dao.stream.discovery.md:70](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/dao.stream.discovery.md:70), [Fable design:224](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1790335900000-architect-dao-stream-serving-spec.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:224) | **med**. **Fable: do not stand** for a public relay. Coupled to Q4.\n\nQ4 | **Alternative: composition-supplied relay admission policy; open admission only in explicitly local or trusted deployments** | `register` allocates a routed peer name and `dial` consumes relay capacity. Postage remains a possible policy, not a settled protocol answer. Relay admission is separate from DaoStream descriptor authorization. | [Fable design:224](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1790335900000-architect-dao-stream-serving-spec.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:224), [dao.stream.discovery.md:159](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/dao.stream.discovery.md:159), [dao.stream.md:285](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/dao.stream.md:285) | **med**. **Fable: do not stand** as a general v1 rule. Depends on Q3’s registration binding.\n\nQ5 | **Alternative: accept OD-3 (a)+(2) and OD-2; revise OD-1 separately; resolve proxy read truth before implementation** | Open result maps already permit a `:retry?` key, so OD-1 is not required for `:establishing`. Its proposed “unknown outcome means nothing appended” rule is unsafe for writes whose effect may be unknown under OD-2. More fundamentally, the proposed proxy returns `blocked` on a cache miss even when the source may hold a value or `gap`, and returns a cached `:newest` instead of the current tail. OD-1–3 do not make those answers satisfy the contract. | [dao.stream.md:109](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/dao.stream.md:109), [dao.stream.md:836](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/dao.stream.md:836), [dao.stream.md:879](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/dao.stream.md:879), [dao.stream.md:479](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/dao.stream.md:479), [dao.stream.md:545](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/dao.stream.md:545), [Fable design:125](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1790335900000-architect-dao-stream-serving-spec.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:125), [Fable design:137](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1790335900000-architect-dao-stream-serving-spec.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:137) | **high**. **Fable: do not stand**; Q5 bundles distinct contract decisions and misses a prerequisite.\n\nQ6 | **Lease-governed** | A served entry needed by a migrated task needs an explicit retirement obligation. Use a separate served-entry lease with a named holder and grantor; it must not govern source retention or silently renew. A renewal sent through a proxy counts only when its required outcome is established under Q1. | [yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:521](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:521), [dao.lease.md:92](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/dao.lease.md:92), [dao.lease.md:202](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/dao.lease.md:202) | **med**. **Fable: stand**, once grant, renewal, and pre-grant lifetime are specified. Depends on Q1 and OD-2.\n\nQ7 | **`dao.stream.serve`; rename today’s `dao.stream.serving` to `dao.stream.serving.copy` or similar** | The present composition forwards source values into socket traffic; the remote reader’s positions belong to its local deposit medium. The rename should accompany correction of WebSocket prose that currently describes attachment to the original stream. | [serving.cljc:234](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/dao/stream/serving.cljc:234), [dao.stream.md:904](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/dao.stream.md:904), [dao.stream.ws.md:18](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/dao.stream.ws.md:18) | **high**. **Fable: stand**; the documentation correction is required regardless of the name."}}
